 "measurement_question": {
  "analysis": "EI = P L^3 / (3 delta) from the linear slope of tip force P vs tip displacement delta.",
  "apparatus": "Clamp the ray base (state whether both hemitrichs or one is clamped; Alben et al. 2007 report ~12x stiffness difference between these), load the free end with a calibrated micro-force transducer (resolution <= 1 microN) or a calibrated cantilever probe, track tip displacement optically (resolution <= 1 micrometre), keep the specimen hydrated, record force-displacement for tip/L < 0.1 (inside the linear range), and repeat with the clamp moved along the ray to get EI(x). Cross-check with micro-CT second moment of area.",
  "decision_rule": "If measured EI >= EI_crit_Nm2 the declared load stays inside the small-deformation limit for this geometry; if EI < EI_crit_Nm2 the linear model is invalid at the declared load and a large-deformation model (or a lower load) is required.",
  "question": "What is the effective flexural rigidity EI (N m^2) of an excised ray of the target fin, as a function of distance from its base, under the clamping condition that matches its in-fin boundary condition, and is it above or below EI_crit_Nm2 of this request?",
  "turns": "the ASSUMED EI range in this package into measured data (>= several rays, with spread)"
 },
